  "title": "Kronecker Input-Gated Rank Adaptation (KiRA) and LoRA Factor Dynamics",
  "summary": "KiRA introduces Kronecker input-gated rank adaptation for parameter-efficient fine-tuning, while LoRA's factor dynamics are studied to determine its impact at low rank. The research highlights the importance of the factor over the band in certain task scenarios.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "KiRA reduces trainable parameters by 8.7--9.7 times compared to low-rank adaptation.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Freezing the output factor B outperforms freezing the input factor A at both bands and ranks.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The factor's influence is supported by 258 primary tests and overlaps with other LoRA variants.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
